            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 57-year-old female patient, admitted on 07/09/2016 with suspected tubal ectopic pregnancy following presentation with lower abdominal pain and vaginal bleeding. On admission, physical examination, transvaginal ultrasonography, and serum beta-hCG measurement confirmed a right-sided tubal ectopic pregnancy without signs of rupture. Intravenous access was established and fluid resuscitation initiated. Given the patient's clinical status and gestational findings, the decision was made for surgical intervention. She underwent laparoscopic salpingectomy with successful removal of the ectopic pregnancy. The postoperative course was uneventful. She was mobilized and discharged home on 09/09/2016 in stable condition. I recommend follow-up with beta-hCG levels to confirm resolution and counseling regarding future fertility. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
